                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "01cacc2f-1943-3461-9864-df9c715e6297",
                        "entry_id": "7c010c4f-438d-3ae7-8e13-6545056bd914",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Action de rendre infantile, d’infantiliser."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "68a7d429-c677-4879-93e4-f698cc70367a",
                                "sense_id": "01cacc2f-1943-3461-9864-df9c715e6297",
                                "text": "La maladie tend à diminuer, à infantiliser. Cette infantilisation est trop souvent accentuée par l’entourage, protecteur, ou les soignants, paternalistes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1cdd9a00-bc02-4c64-b0c8-da7e4d54f573",
                                "sense_id": "01cacc2f-1943-3461-9864-df9c715e6297",
                                "text": "Nos gouvernements ne résistent pas à la tentation de l’infantilisation qui devient exaspérante. Nous aurons droit à une trêve de Noël supervisée par des experts de la Santé publique. Ottawa nous dit même à quel volume mettre la musique."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b56ef73e-b3f3-4534-8507-8843337a1321",
                        "source_entry_id": "7c010c4f-438d-3ae7-8e13-6545056bd914",
                        "source_sense_id": "01cacc2f-1943-3461-9864-df9c715e6297",
                        "target_lang_word": "infantilization",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "infantilization",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9d87b431-063b-3827-bff3-24caf7baa220",
                                        "entry_id": "a3e1511c-59c2-385e-b519-819b2c196ceb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act or process of infantilizing, treating a non-infant as an infant, or more generally treating an adult like a young child."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7a62a0f-56c9-4c88-b357-1317ae2470fe",
                                                "sense_id": "9d87b431-063b-3827-bff3-24caf7baa220",
                                                "text": "Nursing homes lead to an infantilization of the elderly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "749d7de4-3e0e-4b59-b5d8-ce7ea9cce015",
                                                "sense_id": "9d87b431-063b-3827-bff3-24caf7baa220",
                                                "text": "In both cases, a key ingredient has been the drastic infantilization of the national culture: from the pious idea of ‘family reading’ that launched the Bowdlerization of Victorian literature, to the syrupy replica—the family, smiling at its TV—that has put American entertainment to sleep."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9dea8f54-9fa8-4a72-9465-3976f4d2a353",
                                                "sense_id": "9d87b431-063b-3827-bff3-24caf7baa220",
                                                "text": "In the context of asexuality, it has led to the infantilization of people who are aspec, and in a lot of cases has pressured ace people to have sex, simply because they didn’t think not wanting to have sex was an option."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
